{
  "answer": "Retention periods vary depending on the category of data: customer account data is retained as long as the account is active and for seven years after account closure [ac735f6387ca659b3a009e78d98f0118]; customer content data is retained while the account is active and deleted within ninety days of account closure unless specified otherwise [ac735f6387ca659b3a009e78d98f0118]; employee records are kept for the duration of employment and seven years after departure [ac735f6387ca659b3a009e78d98f0118]; security and access logs are retained for one year [ac735f6387ca659b3a009e78d98f0118]; postmortems and incident timelines are retained indefinitely [ac735f6387ca659b3a009e78d98f0118]; database backups are kept for thirty days on a rolling basis [ac735f6387ca659b3a009e78d98f0118]; and aggregated, de-identified analytics data may be retained indefinitely [b27f10fcc77b64d06f491ca98fd343c7].",
  "citations": [
    "ac735f6387ca659b3a009e78d98f0118",
    "b27f10fcc77b64d06f491ca98fd343c7"
