{
  "answer": "Engineers request production database access through the access request form on the internal tools portal, providing the specific database, table or schema, reason, and expected duration [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13]. Approval requires sign-off from the data owner and two engineering managers, with one manager from a different team than the requesting engineer [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13]. All approvals must be recorded in the form, and verbal or chat approvals are insufficient [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13]. Additionally, engineers must have completed the annual security training within the last ninety days [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13]. During an incident, on-call engineers may request break-glass access without waiting for standard approval [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13] [f9cbee4e0939d52e95eebe93a063a85c].",
