{
  "answer": "The Production Database Access SOP describes how engineers request, receive, and lose production database access [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13]. It applies to engineers needing direct read or write access to a production database, such as on-call engineers, those debugging customer issues, or running one-time data migrations, but excludes access through internal admin tools with their own audit logs and approval flows [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13]. Engineers request access via an access request form on the internal tools portal, requiring approval from the system's data owner and two engineering managers (with one from a different team) [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13]. Standard access is granted for three days and expires automatically, and engineers must have completed annual security training within the last ninety days [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13], [fa6a8fa3ff7c9abfd858f139e55ab66d]. During incidents, on-call engineers may request break-glass emergency access without standard approval, which is logged and reviewed the next business day [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13]. All access grants are logged and reviewed weekly by Security Engineering [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13], [91d4f121536a0880dff84e83193cd833]. A manager or data owner can revoke access early [91d4f121536a0880dff84e83193cd833]. Service accounts and automated jobs follow a separate process requiring sign-off from the data owner and two engineering managers, with quarterly reviews rather than automatic expiration [91d4f121536a0880dff84e83193cd833].",
  "citations": [
    "da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13",
    "fa6a8fa3ff7c9abfd858f139e55ab66d",
    "91d4f121536a0880dff84e83193cd833"
  ],
  "sufficient_evidence": true
}

{
  "answer": "During an active incident, an on-call engineer may request break-glass access to production systems without waiting for the standard approval review [e3e91b1f9845f9e5b17e8e375d325dd9] [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13] [f9cbee4e0939d52e95eebe93a063a85c]. This break-glass access does not require the standard approval flow—which normally necessitates sign-off from the data owner and two engineering managers—and is instead granted immediately, logged automatically, posted to the security channel, and reviewed by a security engineer the next business day [e3e91b1f9845f9e5b17e8e375d325dd9] [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13] [f9cbee4e0939d52e95eebe93a063a85c].",
  "citations": [
    "e3e91b1f9845f9e5b17e8e375d325dd9",
    "da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13",
    "f9cbee4e0939d52e95eebe93a063a85c"
  ],
  "sufficient_evidence": true
}

