{
  "answer": "Access to a vendor-managed service like a payment processor's administrative console is approved by the data owner for that integration and one engineering manager [54b5200c0f4ab243c0eb22bd471d9068] [eee7938e3bf0085d571e51f5a07a0389]. It lasts for the standard seven-day grant window from the Production Database Access SOP, unless the vendor's tooling only supports longer-lived credentials, which requires a documented exception and business justification [54b5200c0f4ab243c0eb22bd471d9068] [eee7938e3bf0085d571e51f5a07a0389]. In comparison, standard internal production database access requires sign-off from the system's data owner and two engineering managers (one of whom must be from a different team) and lasts for three days instead of seven [da1cdb5e0e87ad69728e9d2781239d13].",
  "citations": [
